  "english": "28. Thursday. Tone 2 [BK]. Saint Cyriacus and Saint Julitta,\nand Saint Gordius, Saint Polyeuctus, and\nSaint Gregory. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 7 [DZ]: \"Holy are you, Lord of hosts\" (Surp es ter zoruteantsd).\n30. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK]. Saint Athanasius and Saint Cyril,\nand Saint Gregory the Theologian.\n31. Sunday. Tone 8 [DZ]. Fifth Sunday. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 2 [BK]:\n\"Beginningless God\" (Anskizbn astuats). Evening Entrance Hymn Tone 8 [DZ]:\n\"By anticipating the women\" (Kanantsn kankhelov).\n\nAugust\n1. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Saint Vahan of Goghtn,\nand Saint Eugene the Virgin, etc.\n[Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 8 [DK]: \"To You, O God of\nour Fathers\" (Ar kez astuats hartsn merots).\n2. Tuesday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Saints Tryphon, Parsamas, and\nOnuphrius the Hermits.\n4. Thursday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Saint Eugenius, Saint Macarius,\nand others. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 8 [DK]: \"He who [showed] the wondrous\" (Or zhrashapar).\n6. Saturday. Tone 5 [GDZ]. The Holy Ecumenical Council of Ephesus\nof the two hundred Patriarchs.\n7. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Sixth Sunday. Eve [Barekendan]\nof the Fast of the Holy Mother of God. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 3 [EZ]: \"We glorify\nyou\" (Paravoremp zkhez). Evening Entrance Hymn Tone 6 [GK]: \"The Divine\" (Zastuatsayin).\n8. Monday. Tone 8 [DZ]. Fast of the Holy Mother\nof God. [Hymn for the] Lenten Fathers Tone 2 [BZ]: \"He who is awesome\" (Or ahavor).\n14. Sunday. Tone 5 [GDZ]. Assumption of the Holy\nMother of God. The period of non-fasting is three\nweeks.\n24. Wednesday. Tone 8 [DZ]. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 2 [BK]: \"The captive\nchildren\" (Mankunkn gerealk). See this intervening period in the First\nVolume, maintaining the order of the place.\n\nSeptember\n4. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fourth Sunday. Eve [Barekendan]\nof the Fast of the Holy Cross. Evening Entrance Hymn Tone 2 [AK]:\n\"The Lord is risen\" (Yarutsyal tern).\n5. Monday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fast of the Holy Cross. [Hymn for the]\nLenten Fathers Tone 2 [BK]: \"The voice of the children\" (Mankantsn zzayn).\n8. Thursday. Tone 6 [GK]. Feast of the Birth of the Holy\nVirgin from Anna.\n11. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See through to\nthe tenth Sunday in the First\nVolume, maintaining the order of this place.\n23. Sunday. Of Saint Sarkis. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 7 [DZ]: \"Glorifying\" (Paravorelov).\nAnd for the others, see the First\nVolume up to Vardavar [Transfiguration],\nmaintaining the order of this place.\n\nFebruary\n6. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Sunday of Great Lent Eve [Bun Barekendan].\n14. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Day of Fasting. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\nSee according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMarch\n27. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Easter. The Day of the Resurrection of\nChrist our God. See\naccording to the order in the First Volume.\n\nApril\n7. Thursday. Tone 2 [BK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy\nMother of God.\n\nMay\n5. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK]. Day of the Ascension of Christ\ninto Heaven.\n15. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost].\nEve [Barekendan] of the Fast of Elijah.\n22. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. First Sunday. Beginning of the Resurrection\nSundays. See according to the order in\nthe First Volume.\n\nJuly\n3. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Vardavar [Transfiguration of Christ]. The period of non-fasting\nis five weeks. See in the First\nVolume up to the Friday of the third week,\nwhich is the nineteenth day, and\nfor the Saturday, return here, and celebrate these\nfeasts written below, which are after\nthe eight-day feast of the Nativity.\n23. Saturday. Tone 8 [DZ]. Saint Peter the Patriarch,\nSaint Blaise the Bishop, and Saint Abisolom\nthe Deacon.\n24. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fourth Sunday. [Hymn for the] Fathers Tone 2 [BK]: \"Who\nof the heavenly hosts\" (Or yerknayin zinvoruteants). Evening Entrance Hymn Tone 8 [DK]:\n\"When they came\" (Yorzham yekin), and \"The Angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn).\n25. Monday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Saint Anthony the Hermit.\n26. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK]. Saint Theodosius the Emperor, and the\nHoly Children of Ephesus.",
